# S15 — full first-time-user happy path (live-e2e Phase 1 scenario 15,
# M1-546). Invite mint -> consume -> the probation-allowed surface end to end
# (free-form chat stays locked during probation by design, D45 — so the path
# exercises /help, /zcash and /summary as the welcome text advertises).
#
# Host preconditions: 'user' must be UNREGISTERED (prod/live-reset.sh; s03
# also registers 'user', so reset between s03 and this scenario). The /zcash
# step needs the public price endpoint reachable.

# 1. Admin mints a single-use open invite; the code is captured. The --open
#    path is confirm-gated (spec §Admin; live-discovered 2026-07-03).
send dm admin /invite create --adapter simplex --open
expect substring 60000 About to mint an OPEN invite

send dm admin /invite create --open confirm
expect substring 60000 Invite code:
capture code ([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})

# 2. The fresh user registers by sending the captured code (D44).
send dm user ${code}
expect substring 60000 Welcome! You're registered.

# 3. Discovery works for the fresh (probation) user.
send dm user /help
expect substring 60000 Available commands:

# 4. Asset command works during probation; the reply names its source + URL.
send dm user /zcash
expect regex 120000 (?s)source:.*https?://

# 5. /summary from a fresh user with zero subscriptions returns the
#    deterministic no-posts reply (commands.md §Content) — the pipeline ran
#    end to end even though the set is empty.
send dm user /summary -w 24h
expect substring 240000 No posts to summarize yet
